\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Temporal responses of SPRiF across tasks, arranged in three parts with seven subplots. (a) The three upper subplots show SPRiF impulse responses on PS-MNIST, GSC and QTDB, from left to right. (b) The three lower-left subplots show normalized frequency-response magnitudes of the memory states for the same tasks. Shading indicates the distribution range across neurons, not uncertainty across random seeds. Frequency is expressed in cycles per step. (c) The lower-right subplot compares normalized slow-decay responses of SPRiF and ASRNN on GSC and QTDB. Solid curves with open markers denote SPRiF; dashed curves with filled markers denote ASRNN.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:temporal_kernels}{{2}{8}{Temporal responses of SPRiF across tasks, arranged in three parts with seven subplots. (a) The three upper subplots show SPRiF impulse responses on PS-MNIST, GSC and QTDB, from left to right. (b) The three lower-left subplots show normalized frequency-response magnitudes of the memory states for the same tasks. Shading indicates the distribution range across neurons, not uncertainty across random seeds. Frequency is expressed in cycles per step. (c) The lower-right subplot compares normalized slow-decay responses of SPRiF and ASRNN on GSC and QTDB. Solid curves with open markers denote SPRiF; dashed curves with filled markers denote ASRNN}{figure.2}{}}
